1.. Status of the Current Fiscal Year 2025-2026 City Council Work Plan, Development of the Fiscal Year 2026-2027 Work Plan, and Approval of the Prioritization of Pending City Council Requests (No Budget Impact) (City Manager Mirzakhanian).
(Estimated Time: 3 Hrs.)
DISCUSS AND PROVIDE DIRECTION {\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fswiss\fprq2\fcharset0 Arial;}}
{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa160\sl252\slmult1\i\f0\fs22 Mayor Lesser reopened the floor for public comment.\line\line Seeing no requests to speak, Mayor Lesser closed the floor to public comment.\cf1\i0\line\line\cf0\i City Manager Talyn Mirzakhanian introduced the Work Plan and introduced Senior Management Analyst Patricia Matson who began the PowerPoint presentation.\line\line The remainder of the PowerPoint was provided in the following order:\line\line\ul Management Services\ulnone\line Senior Management Analyst Matson presented.\line\line City Manager Mirzakhanian responded to City Council questions.\line\line Councilmember Howorth suggested adding the word \ldblquote challenges\rdblquote  to the City Council Work Plan item so that it reads: \ldblquote Evaluation of Opportunities and Challenges for the City\rquote s Involvement in the 2026 FIFA World Cup and 2028 Summer Olympic Games.\rdblquote  There were no objections.\line\line\ul Finance\ulnone\line Finance Director Libby Bretthauer presented and responded to City Council questions.\line\line\ul Parks and Recreation\ulnone\line Parks and Recreation Director Mark Leyman presented and responded to City Council questions.\line\line\ul Community Development\ulnone\line Community Development Director Masa Alkire presented.\line\line Community Development Director Alkire, Building Official Ryan Heise and Traffic Engineer Erik Zandvliet responded to City Council questions.\line\line Councilmember Charelian suggested adding a notable accomplishment recognizing the City\rquote s updated noticing policy for State Density Bonus and Residential Overlay District projects. There were no objections.\line\line\ul Public Works\ulnone\line Interim Public Works Director Joseph DeFrancesco presented.\line\line City Manager Mirzakhanian, Interim Public Works Director DeFrancesco and City Engineer Gilbert Gamboa responded to City Council questions.\line\line Mayor Lesser opened the floor to public comments. The following individual spoke:\line\line Jim Upchurch\line\line Seeing no further requests to speak, Mayor Lesser closed the floor to public comments.\line\line City Manager Mirzakhanian, Interim Public Works Director DeFrancesco and City Engineer Gamboa responded to City Council questions.\line\line At 7:21 PM, the City Council recessed and reconvened at 7:30 PM with all City Councilmembers present.\line\line City Manager Mirzakhanian made a correction and clarified that the 28th Street Groundbreaking Ceremony is scheduled for Thursday, March 5, 2026, at 11:00 AM.\line\line\ul Human Resources\line\line\ulnone Human Resources Director Lisa Jenkins presented.\line\line\ul Police\ulnone\line Police Chief Rachel Johnson presented.\line\line Police Chief Johnson and City Manager Mirzakhanian responded to City Council questions.\line\line\ul Fire\ulnone\line Fire Chief Jesse Alexander presented.\line\line\ul Information Technology\ulnone\line Information Technology Director Miguel Guardado presented.\line\line Information Technology Director Guardado and Communications and Civic Engagement Manager Alexandria Latragna responded to City Council questions.\line\line\ul Management Services\ulnone\line Senior Management Analyst Matson concluded the Work Plan portion of the meeting and began the PowerPoint presentation on the prioritized list of pending City Council requests, starting with Management Services.\line\line City Manager Mirzakhanian responded to City Council questions.\line\line The remainder of the PowerPoint presentation regarding Pending City Council Requests was presented in the following order:\line\line\ul Finance\ulnone\line Finance Director Bretthauer presented.\line\line City Manager Mirzakhanian and Community Development Director Alkire responded to City Council questions.\line\line\b The City Council directed staff to prepare an annual briefing note on the fiscal impacts of the holiday meter bagging.\line\line\ul\b0 Parks and Recreation\ulnone\b\line\b0 Parks and Recreation Director Leyman presented.\line\line\ul Community Development\line\ulnone Community Development Director Alkire presented.\line\line Community Development Director Alkire, Traffic Engineer Zandvliet and City Manager Mirzakhanian responded to City Council questions.\line\line\b The City Council directed staff to move the Discussion of the Use of a Shuttle Service in the City up from a low priority to a medium priority.\line\line\ul\b0 Public Works\line\ulnone Interim Public Works Director DeFrancesco presented.\line\line Interim Public Works Director DeFrancesco and City Manager Mirzakhanian responded to City Council questions.\line\line\ul Police\ulnone\line Police Chief Johnson presented.\line\line Police Chief Johnson and City Manager Mirzakhanian responded to City Council questions.\line\line\b The City Council directed staff to return with a proposal to establish a diversion program for minors and adults who receive e-bike violations.\line\line\ul\b0 Fire\ulnone\b\line\b0 Fire Chief Alexander presented.\line\line\b The City Council directed staff to bring back the discussion on Emergency Shelter Solutions at a future City Council meeting to help promote and raise community awareness.\line\line\b0 Senior Management Analyst Matson, City Manager Mirzakhanian and Traffic Engineer Zandvliet responded to City Council questions.\line\line\b The City Council directed staff to explore formatting options to restructure the City Council Work Plan, emphasizing each item\rquote s priority and its ability to be completed within the Fiscal Year, and to return with the format that best meets the City Council\rquote s objectives.\b0\line\line\pard The PowerPoint presentation concluded.\par
